id: violent-rebuke
name: Violent Rebuke
order: 4
category: body
importance: secondary
description: >
  Built to withstand the brutal punishment that annihilated the Tuffle race, you can take a hit and dish out one in return.
text: >
  Violent Rebuke (Body): Built to withstand the brutal punishment that annihilated the Tuffle race, you can take a hit and dish out one in return.
  (1)-[Passive]: You may use your Scholarship or Personality Modifier instead of your Force Modifier for the effects of Surgency.
  (2)-[Triggered/Threshold]: If you succeed at the Steadfast Check for this Health Threshold, use a Healing or Ki Surge (you decide) as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (3)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: After completing an Opponent’s Attacking Maneuver that targeted you, regardless of if it hits, you may make a Basic Attack Maneuver against them as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver. You cannot Ki Wager on this Attacking Maneuver unless that Opponent was your Inferior.

---

[passive]
# (1) Whichever of the three is the highest (actor-character.mjs).
allow surgency.scholarshipOrPersonality;
# (3) An Opponent's Attacking Maneuver aimed at you, hit or not: the Basic Attack at them offered on its card out of sequence,
# once a Round - no Ki Wager unless they were this Round's Inferior (chat.mjs offerRebuke).
allow rebuke.strike;

# (2) The Steadfast Check for a Health Threshold passed: chosen in its window - one Out-of-Sequence Maneuver for one trigger -
# a Surge, which asked.
[triggered/steadfast-passed, outOfSequence, effect 2]
surge();
